Let $\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}.$  Then
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} a(2) + b(-1) \\ c(2) + d(-1) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}, \\
\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} a(1) + b(-3) \\ c(1) + d(-3) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
This gives us the system of equations
\begin{align*}
2a - b &= 9, \\
a - 3b &= 7.
\end{align*}
Solving this system, we find $a = 5$ and $b = 2.$  Hence,
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} 5(2) + 2(-1) \\ 5(2) + 2(-1) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}, \\
\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} 5(1) + 2(-3) \\ 5(1) + 2(-3) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
Thus, the image of the line $y = 2x + 1$ under $\mathbf{M}$ is the line $y = 7x - 4.$
