Next, we expand the second product:

\begin{align*}
(u-3)(u+6) &= u^2 + 6u - 3u - 18 \\
&= u^2 + 3u - 18.
\end{align*}

Now, we subtract the second product from the first:

\begin{align*}
(u^2 + 3u - 4) - (u^2 + 3u - 18) &= u^2 + 3u - 4 - u^2 - 3u + 18 \\
&= 17.
\end{align*}

